  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q5",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p33-q5-stem",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Consider the letters of the word RAINBOW. Bob and Mary are tasked to find the number of arrangements such that the word RAIN appears in that order, but with the letters not necessarily together.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p33-q5-bob",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Bob says that you can place RAIN down first, and place the other three letters in to the gaps. After each letter is placed, a new gap opens up. So, there are ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "5\\times6\\times7",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " possible arrangements.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p33-q5-mary",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Mary says that she got the answer by permuting everything ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "7!",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " and then dividing by the number of ways to arrange RAIN, ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "4!",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", so ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\frac{7!}{4!}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ".",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p33-q5-instruction",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Which method is valid?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p33-q5-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Both methods are valid; each gives 210 arrangements.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p33-q5-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Insert the remaining letters into successive gaps, or divide all arrangements by the ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "4!",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " equally frequent relative orders of R, A, I and N.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Both methods are valid.\n\nBob: insert B, O and W in a fixed sequence. RAIN has five gaps, including the two ends. Each inserted letter creates one more gap, so\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=5\\times6\\times7\\\\N&=210.\\end{align*}$$\n\nMary: the $7!$ arrangements contain each of the $4!$ relative orders of R, A, I and N equally often. Only one relative order is allowed, so\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\frac{7!}{4!}\\\\N&=210.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
